{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.QSubstrate","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.wenzlClosedForm_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.wenzlClosedForm_empty","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L249-L257","doc":"The empty partition contributes the bare Markov-parameter prefactor: the\ncell product is empty, so `y_∅(q) = z^{0-1} = z⁻¹`… but `n = 0` here, and\n`0 - 1 = 0` in `ℕ`, so the prefactor is `z^0 = 1`. A sanity check that the\nfold bottoms out rather than a statement about Wenzl's formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.wenzlClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.wenzlClosedForm","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L221-L247","doc":"**Wenzl closed form** for the Jones-Markov coefficient `y_λ(q)`\n(Wenzl 1988 Lemma 3.2):\n\n    y_λ(q) = z^{n-1} · ∏_{(i,j) ∈ λ} [h_{(i,j)}^λ]_q⁻¹ · q^{|λ|·c_{(i,j)}^λ}\n\nwith `z = QSubstrate.markovParameter` the Markov parameter and `[k]_q` the\n`qInteger` above. The product runs over the cells of `λ`: rows\n`i < (partsList λ).length`, and within each row columns `j < λ_i`.\n\n**Transcription note.** The formula is transcribed from this module's own\nheader (the manuscript's statement of Wenzl §3) and has *not* been checked\nagainst Wenzl 1988 independently — in particular the `q^{|λ|·c}` exponent\nconvention (rather than the more common `q^{c}`) is the manuscript's, not\na correction of mine. Making it an explicit definition is what turns the\nidentification below into a checkable claim; verifying the convention\nagainst the source is the remaining task in bean `qou-t7zg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellHookLength_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellHookLength_corner","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L215-L219","doc":"The corner cell `(0,0)` of a nonempty partition has hook length\n`λ₀ + λ'₀ − 1`, the full first row plus the full first column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent_swap","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L210-L213","doc":"**Content is antisymmetric under transposing the cell** — the chirality\natom (cf. `BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneChiralityInvolution`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent_diag","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L206-L208","doc":"A cell on the diagonal has content `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent_apply","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L203-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellHookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellHookLength","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L197-L201","doc":"**Hook length** `h_{(i,j)} = (λ_i − j) + (λ'_j − i) − 1`: the arm to the\nright of `(i,j)`, plus the leg below it, plus the cell itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.cellContent","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L190-L195","doc":"**Cell content** `c_{(i,j)} = j − i` (column index minus row index).\nIndependent of `λ`; the partition argument is kept for call-site symmetry\nwith `cellHookLength`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.colLen","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L185-L188","doc":"Column length `λ'_j = #{ i : λ_i > j }` — the conjugate partition's `j`-th\npart, computed by counting the rows long enough to reach column `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.rowLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.rowLen","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L181-L183","doc":"Row length `λ_i` (`0` past the last row). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.partsList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.partsList","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L177-L179","doc":"The parts of `λ` as a descending list — the row lengths `λ₀ ≥ λ₁ ≥ …`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L153-L158","doc":"The q-integer `[0]_q = 0` (by convention; consistent with\n`[k]_q = (q^{k/2} - q^{-k/2}) / (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})` having\na zero numerator at `k = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger_one","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L139-L151","doc":"`[1]_q = 1` whenever the denominator `q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2}` is\nnon-zero (i.e. for `q ≠ 1`).  At `q = 1` the formula gives\n`0/0 = 0` by Lean's division convention; the `[1]_q = 1`\nidentity is the limit, which Mathlib does not transport\nautomatically.  This is the \"generic-q\" form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L105-L137","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket — this is not a third\nconvention.**\n\nThe half-powers make this site look like a separate `[k]` from both `qIntBal`\nand `qIntGeo`, and an earlier census set it aside on exactly that reading.  It\nis not: substituting `v = q^{1/2}` gives `v^k = q^{k/2}` and\n`v⁻¹ = q^{-1/2}`, so the whole expression is the *balanced* bracket in the\nhalf-power variable.\n\nThat makes it the mirror of `qIntegerRescaled`: one site is the canonical\nbracket at `q²`, this one at `q^{1/2}`, and both are instances of the single\ntwist `qIntBal_eq_twist_canonical` rather than new conventions.  Here the `k = 0`\nguard is again redundant — `qIntBal v 0 = 0` already.\n\n`0 ≤ q` is the real content of the hypothesis: it is what lets `rpow` powers\ncompose (`(q^{1/2})^k = q^{k/2}`), and it is the file's own standing assumption\n(\"Defined for real `q > 0`\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl.qInteger","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovWenzl.lean#L97-L103","doc":"The q-integer `[k]_q := (q^{k/2} - q^{-k/2}) / (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})`.\nEquivalent to the standard `[k]_q = 1 + q + q² + ... + q^{k-1}`\nwhen `q ≠ 1`.  Defined for real `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}